ipt checks measures plan optimality (the pre-study's fold\nand tag counts are byte-identical across horizons). This PR is the\nround-9 replay-speed commission's L0+L1, harness only -- no production\nfile is touched, and outputs are deliberately NOT byte-identical: the\nowner lifted byte identity for this script; purpose fidelity is what the\nproofs below measure.\n\nL0: `replay` returns `{}` when its arm dict is empty; every non-empty arm\nset (the argv-only two-zone arms) still shares the prefix as before.\nL1: `OptimizationConfig` in `start_state` moves horizon_hours 24.0 -> 12.0.\nThe settled house_heat_loss_scale is plan-sensitive and moves with the\nhorizon: 1.0416 -> 1.0480 measured on the shared pre-boost day, so the\nin-script `converged_near` anchor is re-anchored 1.0424 -> 1.0480 (a\ncommit-message-declared re-anchor of an in-script constant, not a golden\nfixture; no claim file is engaged -- the script has none).\n\n## Head\n\n`3318d69b2bc3b3e95cb15e68123f70ee94ffcd6e` is the orchestrator's recarry of main into the previous head. It is not a clean merge of the live head and main (parent 1 0f8d8595 is not the live pull-request head 3318d69b), so prepr checked this head.\n\n`3318d69b2bc3b3e95cb15e68123f70ee94ffcd6e` merges main `cb7cb25` into the previous head: an automatic merge by the orchestrator, no resolution. The reviewed code is unchanged.\n\n0f8d85957\n\n## Mutation proof\n\nAll 11 replay-only ledger anchors, driven by the ledger's own verifier,\n`python3 tests/mutation_table.py --anchor <anchor> --scripts\ntests/boost_drift_replay.py` (full log in the seat scratch,\n`seat/pin-verify.log`; per-anchor commands in ## Figures). 11/11 KILLED.\n\nThe two plants the commission names, KILLED with the same failure counts\nthe ledger recorded at the 24 h horizon:\n\n- P-1935 (`boost.space_learning_frozen` GUARD_OFF 102df8a4): rc=1,\n  4 of 46 checks failed (ledger recorded failed=4) -- folds inside frozen\n  spans and the #1935 band blown.\n- P-tag (`boost.space_boost_active` RETURN_DEL 65ac3dc1): rc=1, 2 of 46\n  failed (ledger recorded failed=2) -- tagging and prediction-suppression\n  checks.\n\nTen of eleven failure counts equal the ledger's recorded counts; one\nkills MORE checks than recorded (`interval_boosted` CMP_BOUND a7932f63:\n2 vs the recorded 1) -- the 12 h horizon makes that boundary additionally\nflip a second check; no pin weakens.\n\nMutations of THIS change, each reddening the acceptance:\n\n- The L0 guard inverted (`if arms:`): the script crashes rc!=0 after\n  re-running the wasted two-zone prefix (`KeyError: 'null_no_boost'`,\n  608 s wall) -- the guard's emptiness condition is load-bearing.\n- The re-anchored constant set wrong (1.0900): `3 of 46 BOOST DRIFT\n  CHECKS FAILED` -- exactly the three per-arm converged-before-boost\n  checks -- the anchor is consulted, not decorative.\n\n## Null control\n\nThe unperturbed tree at HEAD: `ALL 46 BOOST DRIFT CHECKS PASSED` (the\nrun quoted under ## Figures). The null arm converges flat and stays in\nband with no false positive: pre-boost 1.048, boost/recovery days\n1.0504 / 1.0497 / 1.0515, final 1.072, all inside the 5 % band, and the\nboost arms still fold 0 inside frozen spans while folding outside them\nand after the last tail. The instrument's own null control (a\ncomment-only edit) survived every driver in each of the 11 drives.\n\n## Figures\n\n- `PYTHONPATH=tests/hastub python3 tests/boost_drift_replay.py` ->\n  `ALL 46 BOOST DRIFT CHECKS PASSED`, wall 203 s at HEAD (box quiet);\n  536 s at the same patch under box load 27-40; the unpatched script\n  measured 2,356.6 s under the same heavy load (controlled pre-study\n  numbers: -91 s for L0 native, 260.1 -> 107.4 s per arm for L1).\n- `python3 tests/mutation_table.py --anchor 'custom_components/heatpump_optimizer/boost.py:space_learning_frozen GUARD_OFF 102df8a4' --scripts tests/boost_drift_replay.py` -> the drive reports the pin REPRODUCED (KILLED).\n- `python3 tests/mutation_table.py --anchor 'custom_components/heatpump_optimizer/boost.py:space_boost_active RETURN_DEL 65ac3dc1' --scripts tests/boost_drift_replay.py` -> REPRODUCED (KILLED).\n- the same command for each of the other 9 anchors in\n  `tests/mutation_ledger/killed_by/{boost.py,coordinator.py}` naming\n  `tests/boost_drift_replay.py` as `killed_by` -> each REPRODUCED\n  (11/11).\n\n## Red checks\n\nnone\n\n## Forward-carry\n\nnone\n\n## Friction\n\nnone\n\n\n\n","created_at":"2026-10-13T01:18:56Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T16:57:06Z","closed_at":"2026-10-13T16:57:03Z","merged_at":"2026-10-13T16:57:03Z","merge_commit_sha":"17948cc256f18cce27537e974dce17331c8b113b","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2166/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2166/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/issues/2166/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/statuses/3318d69b2bc3b3e95cb15e68123f70ee94ffcd6e","head":{"label":"tvofi:fix/replay-fast","ref":"fix/replay-fast","sha":"3318d69b2bc3b3e95cb15e68123f70ee94ffcd6e","user":{"login":"tvofi","id":70032254,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMDMyMjU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70032254?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi","html_url":"https://github.com/tvofi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvof